 "note": "Solved by tools/guns/sniper.py (SniperHoldSolver over gunkit.HoldSolver). R6: rigid arms; the weld (Right Arm space) is the only wrist (<= 25 deg off GripR / BoltGrip). rightHand / supportHand are the hand points in arm space: on the arm blocks' front faces, so the gun rides against the blocks instead of through their centre lines. Hard limits per stance (checked, see \"check\"): blade and lean within the stance tolerance, Root roll <= 3 deg (the hips only counter pitch), neck pitch <= 25 and roll <= 12, eye within 0.15 stud of the scope line (Aim, BoltCycle; the first-person scope view comes from the camera), feet level on y = -3. BoltCycle: the right hand on the lifted bolt knob (bolt at -60 deg), cheek on the stock. ReloadMag: stock low in the pocket, gun canted 9 deg, the left hand on the seated magazine (MagGrab).",
